To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: Re: DEC PW 500au and Gloria Synergy-8
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=106737353618823

Eric Dillenseger wrote (in a message from Monday 27)
 > Hi,
 > I'm trying to run Xfree on this box but everytime I run it, it hangs
 > eating all the cpu.
 > 
I think a regression was introduced on the X server for VGA cards
between the upgrade to XFree86 4.3 and OpenBSD 3.4. Unfortunatly I
didn't test it enough before the final 3.4 code freeze. I plan to have
a deeper look at it in a few weeks after a couple of other things are
done. 

 > Can I get it working? how?

I guess you can fetch the OPENBSD_3_3 XF4 tree on your system and
rebuild it under -current. (Or even run the 3.3 binaries with the
correct libraries). 


					Matthieu

